# tiny64.dmc — the smallest program that still touches the Forge: one 64-byte,
# no-flags `forge.zeros` allocation. Fixture for tools/rss_gate.py (#825).
#
# #822's first version made a page-aligned `alloc_zeroed` chunk touch all 512
# MiB of the default chunk eagerly, so EVERY `dmc jit` run — no matter how
# small its own allocation — paid the full chunk's pages. This program is
# deliberately trivial: its own live data is 64 bytes, so its peak RSS is
# almost entirely fixed overhead (binary, runtime, Cranelift/interpreter
# startup, the chunk itself if the chunk stops being lazy again). That makes
# it the most sensitive of the three rss_gate probes to exactly the #822
# class of regression, in contrast to attn_grad_jit.dmc's real fused-attention
# workload, whose own live tensors are a much larger share of its peak.
fn main() -> i64 {
    let t = forge.zeros[u8, [64]]
    t[0] as i64
}
